<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Lathi State</h1><p class="st-meta">1340 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Lathi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Gohil Rajput state in Saurashtra, best remembered for its Thakore Sursinhji, the Gujarati poet known as Kalapi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Lathi was ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gohil">Gohil Rajputs</a>, the clan of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bhavnagar-state">Bhavnagar</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/palitana-state">Palitana</a>; tradition dates its founding to the 14th century. Little is recorded of its early history.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Lathi was a minor state of a few villages in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar-agency">Kathiawar Agency</a>. Its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalapi">Sursinhji Gohil</a> (1874–1900) wrote romantic Gujarati poetry under the name Kalapi, and his collection <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalapino-kekarav">Kalapino Kekarav</a> made him one of the leading poets of modern Gujarati literature.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Lathi joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saurashtra-state">United State of Saurashtra</a> in 1948 and is now a town in Amreli district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lathi-state.jpg" alt="Lathi State" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Unknown, person in image himself died in 1900 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sursinhji_Gohil_Kalapi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1340 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lathi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sursinhji (Kalapi)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lathi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1644&amp;focus=lathi-state" aria-label="Lathi State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6595 1375 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lathi State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6915 1631L7364 1601M6915 1631L7364 1602M6915 1631L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6915 1631h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6915 1631h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1644&amp;focus=lathi-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
